WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Now let's add a new women-owned brand.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Open The Switch, then the Add a brand tab.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
There are five steps: Brand, Owner and proof, Shopping, Products, and Review and publish.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Start with the brand's website.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Press Fetch. It reads her store, finds her products, and checks for an affiliate program.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Here it found four products. They'll wait at step four.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.000
The name, description and logo were filled in for you. Always check them.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Add a one-line story, in our own words.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Your work saves as you type. Nothing is public until you publish.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Step two, Owner and proof. This is the most important step.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Enter the owner's full name, first and last.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Then the share that's women-owned.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.000
The date you checked her ownership.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.000
The kind of evidence you found.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
And the link where you saw it. Use a real link or a named document, never just a note.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Where she's based.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.000
And the founder's email, so she can be sent the certification invitation.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Step three, Shopping. Choose how clicks are paid. Direct means no affiliate network yet.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Payout details are greyed out. Those are the owner's.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.000
And where her products ship from.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Step four, Products. Here are the four products Fetch found.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Each one gets a product type and a short why line. Ready means it can publish.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Under the table, choose her category. You can use the suggestion.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Step five, Review and publish. Everything is in one list.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Green means done. Grey means optional.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.000
The owner certification invitation goes out once the brand is live. If the button is greyed out for you, the owner sends it.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Publish checks everything one more time, then her products go live.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.000
And that's it.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Her products are published, and the brand now shows as live. In this demo, nothing really went live.
